<title>USA: NeoMagic IPO price range raised to $9-$11.</title>
<headline>NeoMagic IPO price range raised to $9-$11.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price of shares in the initial public offering of NeoMagic Corp has been raised to a range of $9 to $11 from its original estimated price range of $7 to $9.</p>
<p>The change was made in a regulatory filing and was confirmed by lead underwriter Morgan Stanley. Three million shares will be sold in the IPO, which is expected to price Thursday for trading on Friday on the Nasdaq under the symbol &quot;NMGC&quot;.</p>
<p>The Santa Clara, California company makes multimedia accelerator solutions for notebook personal computer manufacturers.</p>
